                            sling:resourceType="weekender/components/contentfragment"
                            displayMode="singleText"
                            elementNames="itinerary"
                            fragmentPath="/content/dam/weekender-shared/en/adventures/gastronomic-marais-tour/gastronomic-marais-tour"
                            text="Gastronomic Marais Tour We meet at ten by the oldest covered market in Paris, and begin with coffee and a croissant still warm from the oven of a baker two streets away. From there the walk follows the guide's own shopping route: a cheese shop where we taste five cheeses from mild to strong, a stall in the old Jewish quarter for falafel, a charcuterie, and a chocolate maker who lets visitors into the workshop. Between stops there are courtyards and a seventeenth-century square to see. We end at about three around a table in a wine bar, with a glass and whatever we bought along the way."
                            variationName="master">
